  "index_algorithm": "One private primitive, three public wrappers:

```rust
fn leaf_for(&self, i: usize) -> &[T] {          // caller guarantees i < size
    let to = self.tail_off();
    if i >= to { return &self.tail; }           // tail region
    let mut node: &Node<T> = &self.root;
    let mut level = self.shift;
    while level > 0 {                           // LOOP, not recursion: depth-safe by construction
        match node { Branch(ch) => node = &ch[(i >> level) & MASK],
                     Leaf(_)    => break }      // unreachable; degrade rather than UB
        level -= BITS;
    }
    match node { Leaf(v) => v, Branch(_) => &[] }
}
pub fn get(&self, i: usize) -> Option<&T> {
    if i >= self.size { return None; }
    self.leaf_for(i).get(i & MASK)              // total: no unwrap, no unchecked indexing
}
```
- `get` is total and never panics; every internal caller uses it (or `leaf_for`).
- `impl Index<usize> for Vector<T>` is the `operator[]` equivalent and panics on OOB with the idiomatic message `index out of bounds: the len is {size} but the index is {i}`. immer's `operator[]` on OOB is UB, so a deterministic panic is a strict improvement and is the documented contract. The driver never reaches it (it iterates `0..v.len()`).
- `first()`/`last()` delegate to `get`; `last` must guard `size == 0` BEFORE computing `size - 1` (otherwise debug underflow panic / release wraparound).
