- `pub fn iter(&self) -> Iter<'_, T>` plus `impl<'a, T> IntoIterator for &'a Vector<T> { type Item = &'a T; type IntoIter = Iter<'a, T>; }` so `for x in &v` works — the faithful, allocation-free analogue of C++ `for (auto x : v)` (C++ `auto x` copies; do NOT require `T: Copy` in Rust).
